{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions","id":973684,"title":"What is your favorite Traditions/Conventions?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-20T22:44:54-07:00","id":973684,"title":"What is your favorite Traditions/Conventions?","content":"What do you like the most?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T23:41:31-07:00","id":973692,"title":"","content":"Dreamspeakers, and other mages that give meaning to dreams.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T23:42:38-07:00","id":973693,"title":"","content":"Could've sworn this post had already been done, but couldn't find it.<br /> <br /> My favorite is the Cult of Ecstasy, because of their combination of mysticism and earthiness. I like the Verbena for the same reason. The Dreamspeakers have that too, but they're too far removed from a modern paradigm for my taste. I'd still play one, but they're not in my top three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T03:06:23-07:00","id":973738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973693#post973693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could've sworn this post had already been done, but couldn't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is!<br /> <br /> It's here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/123612-favorite-tradition-paradigm\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ition-paradigm</a><br /> <br /> Best to perform some thread necromancy, before we have two full duplicates.<br /> <br /> <br /> @mods: Can you merge this one into, well, that one?<br /> <br /> And before I forget it...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions#post973684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you like the most?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one do you like the most?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:21:51-07:00","id":973749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973738#post973738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which one do you like the most?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Order of Hermes(among the Tradition) and The Syndicate(among the Technocracy) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The Society of Ether and The Void Engineers are the close seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-21-2016, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:49:36-07:00","id":973756,"title":"","content":"Hermetics and Etherites among the Traditions. Void Engineers among the Technocracy. Taftani among the Disparates. I really like the way they focus on the possibility and majesty of Magic (or Science! as the case may be).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T04:59:25-07:00","id":973760,"title":"","content":"I really like all of them! Seriously, each of them have really good things going for them in terms of ideals, and the bad things serve to create really interesting complex characters.<br /> <br /> That being said, I did myself naturally drawn to Verbena since my mother was an actual witch who used to practice herblore and introduced me to crystals and tarot, call it a soft spot if you will.<br /> <br /> I love the Sons of Ether though, very first character I ever played was an Etherite so I can't help but be interested in how things apply to them when I read.<br /> <br /> Euthanatos is so much fun, their sense of morality is so understandable yet brilliantly flawed that they become really interesting debate partners, and the subtle danger behind them going rogue keeps you on your toes.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes, the most self important of the bunch, I enjoy them for their rigid hierarchy and academic approach to magic, and how on the surface they seem to be most snobby of mages, when if you dig deeper they have one of the most diverse collections of disciplines of all the traditions. Such a wonderful contrast of expectations.<br /> <br /> Conventions wise, I don't think there's a convention I don't like.<br /> NWO are the idealist socialists who drive their agenda via absolute surveillance and control of information. They are big brother and the MiB rolled into one, and while their practices are downright scary, their goal is all too human.<br /> <br /> Syndicate, these bastards are just brilliant! The conservative capitalists who are more concerned with the status quo than any of the others, and serve as the perfect anchor for the other conventions more ambitious groups. They are ruthless, they are uncaring, and at times they are illegal, and that's what makes them great!<br /> <br /> Void engineers are probably the most level headed and least hedonistic of all the conventions, and there new militarised version makes them feel more sober than before. They are the most tragic convention and get the least respect and the most suspicion from their colleagues. Also, space marines! What's not to love.<br /> <br /> I'll admit I haven't read the convention book or the Progenitors or the Iterators just yet, so I can't talk about them much, but I'm already predisposed to liking the Progenitors because I've been studying biomedical science for most of my life, and I see a lot of parallels between the way they organise themselves and the way real left medical science operates here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:08:23-07:00","id":973764,"title":"","content":"With the Traditions I'm generally happy with most but have issues with two. The Verbena could use a rewrite to make them less &quot;Wicca is super true&quot; with perhaps divisions based on something more real world than what was given(Like Slavs, vs Germanic, vs Celts etc). Virtual adepts seem more and more weirdly superfluous.<br /> <br /> Technocracy, I find the Harder Science Conventions easier to play, but still love the role Syndicate and NWO have as npcs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T05:29:26-07:00","id":973771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973764#post973764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Verbena could use a rewrite to make them less &quot;Wicca is super true&quot; with perhaps divisions based on something more real world than what was given(Like Slavs, vs Germanic, vs Celts etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's literally the conceit they're based on. The Margaret Murray pan-European witch cult is real.<br /> <br /> Being realistic would mean they just don't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:02:34-07:00","id":973787,"title":"","content":"The Order of Hermes. I love how complete their Tradition is and their academic approach on magick. Ina second place, the Etherites. Akashics in third.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T06:47:12-07:00","id":973823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973760#post973760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like all of them! Seriously, each of them have really good things going for them in terms of ideals, and the bad things serve to create really interesting complex characters.<br /> <br /> That being said, I did myself naturally drawn to Verbena since my mother was an actual witch who used to practice herblore and introduced me to crystals and tarot, call it a soft spot if you will.<br /> <br /> I love the Sons of Ether though, very first character I ever played was an Etherite so I can't help but be interested in how things apply to them when I read.<br /> <br /> Euthanatos is so much fun, their sense of morality is so understandable yet brilliantly flawed that they become really interesting debate partners, and the subtle danger behind them going rogue keeps you on your toes.<br /> <br /> Order of Hermes, the most self important of the bunch, I enjoy them for their rigid hierarchy and academic approach to magic, and how on the surface they seem to be most snobby of mages, when if you dig deeper they have one of the most diverse collections of disciplines of all the traditions. Such a wonderful contrast of expectations.<br /> <br /> Conventions wise, I don't think there's a convention I don't like.<br /> NWO are the idealist socialists who drive their agenda via absolute surveillance and control of information. They are big brother and the MiB rolled into one, and while their practices are downright scary, their goal is all too human.<br /> <br /> Syndicate, these bastards are just brilliant! The conservative capitalists who are more concerned with the status quo than any of the others, and serve as the perfect anchor for the other conventions more ambitious groups. They are ruthless, they are uncaring, and at times they are illegal, and that's what makes them great!<br /> <br /> Void engineers are probably the most level headed and least hedonistic of all the conventions, and there new militarised version makes them feel more sober than before. They are the most tragic convention and get the least respect and the most suspicion from their colleagues. Also, space marines! What's not to love.<br /> <br /> I'll admit I haven't read the convention book or the Progenitors or the Iterators just yet, so I can't talk about them much, but I'm already predisposed to liking the Progenitors because I've been studying biomedical science for most of my life, and I see a lot of parallels between the way they organise themselves and the way real left medical science operates here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Splendid reviews. You magnificently captured each Convention's charms and appeals. Indeed, they are all individual, pleasant and attractive. <br /> <br /> Just a nitpick - I have thought the Syndicate is always the most despised, underestimated and belittled among the Technocratic Conventions...?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","user":"Posthumanity","date":". 09-21-2016, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:06:29-07:00","id":973834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973823#post973823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Splendid reviews. You magnificently captured each Convention's charms and appeals. Indeed, they are all individual, pleasant and attractive.<br /> <br /> Just a nitpick - I have thought the Syndicate is always the most despised, underestimated and belittled among the Technocratic Conventions...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you!<br /> <br /> I agree with you. NWO consider themselves more powerful than Syndicate, and the other conventions belittle dispatchers as little more than glorified accountants. The Syndiacte know this, and totally own it though. They use this underestimation to keep a low profile while they keep an eye on everything the other conventions try to do. After all, if they want any kind of financing, they're going to have to explain their pitch. Syndicate members know how to get things done at a street level. While the NWO takes the government approach, and the other three barge in with their respective diciplines, the Syndicate act more like a virus, they implant their people subtly and slowly turn each new venture into one of their own.<br /> <br /> So while most of the other conventions consider the Syndicate to be petty criminals and ego inflated business guys, the reality is that the Syndicate probably have much more influence on the direct lives of sleepers than any of the other conventions could imagine. Their only major failing is that they become just as vulnerable as the masses do when any big sweeping changes occur, giving them a natural incentive to keep everything as fixed as possible, stifling themselves as much as they do the other conventions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:54:27-07:00","id":973849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973834#post973834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you!<br /> <br /> I agree with you. NWO consider themselves more powerful than Syndicate, and the other conventions belittle dispatchers as little more than glorified accountants. The Syndiacte know this, and totally own it though. They use this underestimation to keep a low profile while they keep an eye on everything the other conventions try to do. After all, if they want any kind of financing, they're going to have to explain their pitch. Syndicate members know how to get things done at a street level. While the NWO takes the government approach, and the other three barge in with their respective diciplines, the Syndicate act more like a virus, they implant their people subtly and slowly turn each new venture into one of their own.<br /> <br /> So while most of the other conventions consider the Syndicate to be petty criminals and ego inflated business guys, the reality is that the Syndicate probably have much more influence on the direct lives of sleepers than any of the other conventions could imagine. Their only major failing is that they become just as vulnerable as the masses do when any big sweeping changes occur, giving them a natural incentive to keep everything as fixed as possible, stifling themselves as much as they do the other conventions.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think the Syndicate still deeply wishes to advance humanity and achieve Technocratic utopia, rather than freeze world into current status. So I consider they were, and is, collaborating with other Conventions to reach their goal of the Global Empowerment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11780-posthumanity","name":"Posthumanity","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T07:58:04-07:00","id":973853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973849#post973849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think the Syndicate still deeply wishes to advance humanity and achieve Technocratic utopia, rather than freeze world into current status. So I consider they were, and is, collaborating with other Conventions to reach their goal of the Global Empowerment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the other thing about the Syndicate, and actually all the conventions and traditions. They are filled with people who have different ideals and interpretations of the doctrine they've been presented with. So absolutely there will be Syndicate members with that goal in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T08:40:52-07:00","id":973874,"title":"","content":"The Solificati! Modern day alchemists and psychonauts with a wee bit more control than the Ecstatics. Outside of the actual faction that joined the OoH and because a House within it, as a Craft/Disparate/Former Tradition, they're OoH-lite, all the ritual, half the snobbery. Their focus on self-perfection through purification and testing also makes them similar to Akashics, but without the self-denial. Sometimes, I get a real Fullmetal vibe from them. They're also down for a good party.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I love the Dreamspeakers, as they're really the only faction with claims closest to any kind of universal &quot;truth.&quot; The spirit world and spirits are a real thing, and we really need to figure out how to deal with them, because a spiritually dead world is a terribly bleak, and possibly <i>actually</i> dead world. I also dig the idea of making deals and bargains with spirits, up to and including allowing themselves to be possessed. I have a concept that might take some house-ruling, but it would be cool to play a shaman that gets ridden by various spirits for various effects. While being ridden, the mage loses access to Sphere magick entirely, but gains bonuses and possibly even Charms depending on the inhabiting spirit. Ferocity and dexterity from wolf spirit, stam, strength, and maybe some additional health/soak from a bear, and possibly burning touch and minor control of flames from a fire spirit. It's possibly game breaking, I know, but if its balanced by the loss of magick while being inhabited as well as some drawbacks (looking more bestial, Willpower penalties, social penalties, altered perceptions, etc), as well as needing to keep the spirit happy through tasks, minor or major, I think it could work. Also, the mage would need that spirit to be present and available, and bottling up a spirit for later use would be awfully rude without making a deal beforehand, and Umbrood are the gossipy type. Word will get around.<br /> <br /> Spirit can be an awfully broken Sphere if allowed to be, but it also comes with all kinds of inconvenient drawbacks, catches, and caveats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:07:53-07:00","id":973883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973874#post973874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit can be an awfully broken Sphere if allowed to be, but it also comes with all kinds of inconvenient drawbacks, catches, and caveats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very true. In theory you can replicate all the other spheres effects with Spirit simply by knowing who to talk to. The biggest downside is reputation. The more you rely on the spirits, the more they expect from you in return, and the moment your goals deviate from theirs, say goodbye to god-like powers and hello to a whole mess of problems. Also, spirits have their own internal rivalry going on, and striking a deal with one brood may make other broods look unfavourably upon you. The spirit sphere makes the most use out of those social attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T09:20:47-07:00","id":973891,"title":"","content":"The two Traditions I've played more than any other are the Etherites and Hermetics, I've enjoyed others but those two are the well I keep coming back to. I've only played Technocracy on two occasions, but I equally enjoyed playing the Void Engineers and the Syndicate and if given the chance would probably roll one of those two again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T10:18:00-07:00","id":973918,"title":"","content":"Mine are Cultists of Ecstasy - because they do their Magick to the fullest as an extension of their lives and who they are. And it's just so appropriate that their Sphere is Time. I have experienced it myself, that when one truly enjoys and values moments, the understanding and sense of what an hour and a minute are, is extremely fluid; this is also visible in procrastination and not getting up from bed for hours :-P.<br /> <br /> And NWO, because trying to do Entropy and Mind (and other Spheres) Effects through 'mere' choice of words, behaviors, analysis and preparation is the highest hallmark of mental skills and discipline that one might have.<br /> <br /> I also like the Nephandi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 09-21-2016, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T11:18:52-07:00","id":973934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Posthumanity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973823#post973823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a nitpick - I have thought the Syndicate is always the most despised, underestimated and belittled among the Technocratic Conventions...?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. The Convention books claim that the VEs and Progenitors both tend to be more in favour of them over the NWO. They may be arrogant but they're not paranoid secret policemen with an army of killer magic cyborgs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:01:24-07:00","id":973962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973934#post973934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not exactly. The Convention books claim that the VEs and Progenitors both tend to be more in favour of them over the NWO. They may be arrogant but they're not paranoid secret policemen with an army of killer magic cyborgs.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always viewed the Syndicate as being pretty squarely in the middle of the Technocracy's scale-of-gray. This is an entirely personal perspective that I make no claim to being objectively true, but I usually rank the Conventions &quot;ethically&quot; from Void Engineers -&gt; Progenitors -&gt; Syndicate -&gt; Iteration X -&gt; NWO (most to least)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 09-21-2016, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T12:48:10-07:00","id":973983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973962#post973962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always viewed the Syndicate as being pretty squarely in the middle of the Technocracy's scale-of-gray. This is an entirely personal perspective that I make no claim to being objectively true, but I usually rank the Conventions &quot;ethically&quot; from Void Engineers -&gt; Progenitors -&gt; Syndicate -&gt; Iteration X -&gt; NWO (most to least)</div> </div> </div> </div>Although I generally agree, the Syndicate book is so insufferably smug, I'd be tempted to go with the fascist thought-police.<br /> <br /> It-X are kinda interesting. I think their convention book wants to portray them as the a-political scientists. There's a recurring theme that they're individually quite nice people, their flaw is that they don't question the authority of the NWO. 'Course, then the later books bring up the Computer again and we get back into the traditional dodgy territory.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T13:39:04-07:00","id":974006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973983#post973983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although I generally agree, the Syndicate book is so insufferably smug, I'd be tempted to go with the fascist thought-police.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely is. The only reason I give them an even shrift is because of their dissident faction. Even they're basically smug Randian objectivists , but at least their ego and religious reverence for free market principles lets them struggle through the conditioning enough to question Control's authority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:39:27-07:00","id":974071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973771#post973771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's literally the conceit they're based on. The Margaret Murray pan-European witch cult is real.<br /> <br /> Being realistic would mean they just don't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Celestial Chorus is built on the Universality of Monotheism but has breaks based on Religious differences, along with personal activities and holding to &quot;Old ways&quot; monothesists like Mithrasists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:24:36-07:00","id":974097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=974071#post974071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Celestial Chorus is built on the Universality of Monotheism but has breaks based on Religious differences, along with personal activities and holding to &quot;Old ways&quot; monothesists like Mithrasists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, but that's based on real-life existing divisions. The Verbena are based on the Wicca myth that there's this pan-European witch cult that all have this single mythology and survived Christianity. In reality, that didn't happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T16:53:41-07:00","id":974112,"title":"","content":"For the Traditions, the Order of Hermes. I've taken a shine to all the others at one point or another, but the Hermetics will always hold a special place in my heart. I learned about Hermetic theory from Vampire, and I've had opportunities to sample aspects of the real life esoteric theory the Order is based on. Plus, there's just something about the ethos and style of the High Ritual Magicians that appeals to me.<br /> <br /> For the Technocracy, I find myself coming back to the Syndicate, funnily enough. There's just something about focusing Enlightened Will through Economics that's really fascinating.<br /> <br /> For the Disparates, it's a toss up between the Wu Lung, the Taftani, and the Solificati.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T20:50:56-07:00","id":974211,"title":"","content":"I tend to like the Virtual Adepts and Iteration X (both of whom I identify with philosophically IRL) and... well.<br /> <br /> *glances at his forum avatar*<br /> <br /> There might be one other I find exceptional resonance with.<br /> <br /> Of course, most of them have interesting ideas behind the faction and variants, I just find it easier to handle the above three's core paradigms in all their variations. While my autism-induced superpowers are potent, they come with commensurate drawbacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T01:03:49-07:00","id":977655,"title":"","content":"Cult of Ecstasy and the Hollow Ones","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2456-zeroninja","name":"zeroninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"87"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T09:56:07-07:00","id":977816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973962#post973962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always viewed the Syndicate as being pretty squarely in the middle of the Technocracy's scale-of-gray. This is an entirely personal perspective that I make no claim to being objectively true, but I usually rank the Conventions &quot;ethically&quot; from Void Engineers -&gt; Progenitors -&gt; Syndicate -&gt; Iteration X -&gt; NWO (most to least)</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I've generally placed it roughly in this order, Void Engineers -&gt; Iteration X (Post Avatar Storm) -&gt; NWO -&gt; Progenitors -&gt; Iteration X (Pre-Avatar Storm) -&gt; Syndicate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=973983#post973983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It-X are kinda interesting. I think their convention book wants to portray them as the a-political scientists. There's a recurring theme that they're individually quite nice people, their flaw is that they don't question the authority of the NWO. 'Course, then the later books bring up the Computer again and we get back into the traditional dodgy territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never really got that vibe at all. Rather I got the vibe that they were intensely, militantly political. The entire convention identifies itself by service to the Technocracy. While the Void Engineers and Syndicate and whatnot are all plotting and scheming and sort of acting in their conventions best interest. Iteration X puts the Technocracy first. They are, and have been for ages, THE foot soldiers of the ascension war. The NWO has traditionally focused on conversion rather than killing. And the Iterators were there for the opposite.<br /> <br /> They are, from top to bottom, a convention that has built itself to pick up the slack that the other conventions have dropped because of their scheming. They build the equipment. They make the primium, they fight the wars. They neither have the time nor the inclination to be 'nice'. Because if they stop.... well the war falters.<br /> <br /> And then the pogrom ends. And the computer disappears. You have a convention that has for so long, set aside personal ambitions in order to focus on getting things done.... no longer needing to get things done. A convention who's members include thousands upon thousands of soldiers, suddenly with no enemies to fight. So what do they do? They go looking for one. Iterators post avatar storm are both spoiling for a fight, and suddenly given much more time to think about the morality of what they're doing.<br /> <br /> Though, depending on the Era, whether that makes them jackbooted thugs or power-armored paladins is anyones guess.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T10:08:24-07:00","id":977819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/973684-what-is-your-favorite-traditions-conventions?p=977816#post977816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never really got that vibe at all. Rather I got the vibe that they were intensely, militantly political. The entire convention identifies itself by service to the Technocracy. While the Void Engineers and Syndicate and whatnot are all plotting and scheming and sort of acting in their conventions best interest. Iteration X puts the Technocracy first.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what being apolitical actually means. It doesn't mean you have no position, it means you don't concern yourself with the formulation of that position. Look at real life armies, they tend to be at least nominally apolitical; that doesn't mean they don't pursue a political agenda, it means they abdicate control of that agenda to their controlling government.<br /> <br /> 'Putting the Technocracy first' means not questioning why the NWO want a legion of Hit Marks built.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}